/**
 * THE INGREDIENT SHEET
 *
 * One picture holding all 49 ingredients in a 7x8 grid, sliced by index.
 * A sheet rather than 49 files because separately drawn icons do not match each
 * other — different light, weight and scale — and reconciling them takes longer
 * than drawing them. One picture is consistent by construction.
 *
 * The supplied sheet carries a printed label under each icon. Those are trimmed
 * off here rather than hidden in CSS: the game prints the ingredient's real name
 * beside the icon already, and at 34px a second baked-in name is an unreadable
 * smudge. The grid was measured off the file (columns every 137px from x=0, rows
 * every 137px from y=8, label band from 115px) rather than assumed.
 *
 * Embedded as a data URI because the game ships as one self-contained page whose
 * CSP blocks external images — a file in public/ works on the dev server and
 * shows nothing once published.
 *
 * ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. This list is the source order of the ingredient arrays
 * as they are concatenated in constants.ts, and the sheet was drawn to match it.
 * Adding an ingredient means appending here AND adding a cell, in the same place.
 */
export const SHEET_COLS = 7;
export const SHEET_CELL_W = 138;
export const SHEET_CELL_H = 138;

